  "scientific_conclusion": "Across 4 grouped cross-validation folds on the development data, the zero-correction pure sensor baseline and regularized residual models produce virtually indistinguishable cross-validated errors (differing by < 0.1 ug/m3). Higher regularization (lambda = 0.1) shrinks residual delta toward zero, effectively matching the robust sensor baseline. This confirms that the visual image branch does not provide consistent out-of-sample predictive gains across groups, and any apparent test improvement on N=97 is well within cross-validation error variance."
